From: RDNA4 local integration
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve constant-space addresses and encoded resource copies

Select physical addressing for reconstructed constant-space memory pointers,
including constant offsets and helper consumers, using the same structural
memory-use test as device-space pointers. Texture/sampler operations alone and
null comparisons keep their existing address model. Handle both address spaces
when storing raw or typed 64-bit pointer payloads.

This fixes raw store for Ptr(2) for device argument-buffer copies mixed with
constant-pointer offset/read/writeback. Thread/constexpr sampler stores still
have no device payload and remain rejected. GPU token-to-descriptor consumption
is separate.

